@startuml Topic2_Tool_Use_Lifecycle
' ============================================================
' TOPIC 2: The Tool Use Lifecycle (the roundtrip)
' TRAP: The MODEL never executes the tool — the APP does.
' ============================================================
title Topic 2 — Tool Use Lifecycle\n(One tool call = one ROUNDTRIP. Model REQUESTS, App EXECUTES.)

skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

actor "User" as U
participant "Your Application\n(developer's code)" as App
participant "Model (LLM)\n(emits tokens only)" as LLM
participant "Tool\n(API / DB / code)" as Tool

== 1. Request (App sends definitions) ==
U -> App: "Should I bring an umbrella in London?"
App -> LLM: user message + **TOOL DEFINITIONS**\n(name, description, input schema)
note right of App
  Developer SENDS the tool definition
  inside the request. Description quality
  drives whether/how the model uses it.
end note

== 2. Model decides -> TOOL CALL ==
LLM --> App: stop_reason = **"tool_use"**\n+ **tool_use block**\n(get_weather, city="London")
note left of LLM
  Model does NOT run anything.
  It only REQUESTS the call.
end note

== 3. Application EXECUTES (client tool) ==
App -> Tool: actually call get_weather("London")
Tool --> App: "rainy, 16C"

== 4. Return result (OBSERVATION) ==
App -> LLM: **tool_result block** = "rainy, 16C"\n(+ full prior context)

== 5. Model continues ==
LLM --> App: final text:\n"Yes, bring an umbrella."
App -> U: reply

note over App, Tool
  == CLIENT vs SERVER TOOLS ==
  * **Client tool**: YOUR app executes (e.g. weather API)
  * **Server tool**: Anthropic executes on their side
    (e.g. web search) — you run nothing
  ----
  == WORKFLOW vs ROUNDTRIP judgment ==
  Pre-fetch (skip roundtrip) when: you ALWAYS need it
  AND already know the inputs.
  Use the roundtrip when: (a) need is uncertain,
  (b) inputs only known at runtime, (c) multi-step/adaptive.
end note

@enduml
